# API structure

Phase 1 `api-identity` is complete. Do not add identity scope or reopen its slices. Its plan remains `api/.cursor/plans/api-identity.md`.

Phase 2 catalog work follows `docs/phases/phase-2/phase-2-status.md`. Read the current stage plan in `api/.cursor/plans/` before writing that stage. Do not start a later stage, and do not start a later slice, until the previous slice's checks exist.

Phase 3 exam work follows `docs/phases/phase-3/phase-3-status.md`. Phase 2's phone exit and browser exit do not block it. Read that stage's plan, test list, and rule before writing it. The exam feature uses package `exams`. Do not put exam nodes on a course tree.

When a slice's checks finish, update `api/.cursor/progress/<stage>/slice-<number>-<name>.md` before starting the next slice. Record what was done, what was tested and the result, any failure and why, and what is next. Keep it short when the tests passed.

Organize code by feature under `com.coachingcenter.api`. Identity stays in `common`, `auth`, and `users`. Catalog features use their own packages (`courses`, `library`, `purchases`, `files`). The exam module uses `exams`. Keep each feature's controller, service, repository, and DTOs inside that feature. Do not add a global `controllers`, `services`, or `repositories` package.

Schema changes go through Flyway only. Keep `ddl-auto=validate`.

Every error body has `code`, `message`, optional `fieldErrors`, `timestamp`, and `requestId`. One `code` names one condition. List endpoints use `page` and `size` and one shared page envelope.

All paths are under `/api/v1`. Do not log secrets, passwords, tokens, or one-time codes.
